comments[27]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-14T09:26:13.424Z",codex-toolchain-1114b,"Baseline current pm-cli 2026.11.14 and pm-changelog 2026.11.13 reproduces corpus.test.ts: 7 pass, 7 fail, including all four named scenarios plus containment rechecks, bounded fits and no-git training. GH-1665 normalizes declared spellings to camel-case SDK keys; underscore options are undeclared, so required-option validation precedes the handler. Keep every filesystem refusal and race witness using supported SDK keys; add explicit host refusal/no-write checks. The historical failed CI log also shows required-option message assertions in domain, benchmark, lineage and loop tests; reproduce and adapt those without weakening matchers. Only this tracker item is owned; recursive-training items remain untouched."
  "2026-11-14T09:35:51.273Z",codex-toolchain-1114b,"Installed public SDK declarations in sdk/extension/command-options.d.ts document canonical camel-case keys, direct spelling normalization and required/unknown validation. Two synthetic pm-cli 2026.11.14 probes are upstream candidates, not filed: (1) a missing required flag yields PmCliError with exitCode 2 but code undefined and context {}, so exact message plus absent-code plus no-write witnesses replace handler-message assertions; (2) a declared required fromTracker plus undeclared typo or from_tracker is dispatched with both keys, despite unknown-option refusal being documented. Canonical handler reads ignore those undeclared values and remain correct if a future host refuses them first. Searches for extension required option code and unknown_option harness returned no issues. The npm artifact omits CHANGELOG.md; reviewed the exact v2026.11.14 source changelog through 2026.11.8, including all new Migrate notes. No setup-phase linked tests are added, preserving tracker-reader compatibility."
  "2026-11-14T09:44:21.235Z",codex-toolchain-1114b,"| Failure | Cause | Fix |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| corpus exclusive publication handles a real concurrent creator and preserves other IO errors | GH-1665 canonical SDK option keys; underscore-only input fails required-option validation before dispatch | use fromTracker; retain exclusive wx publication, real concurrent creator, ENOENT/ENOTDIR and other IO witnesses |\n| corpus missing or invalid directories refuse with stable path-free errors before inventory reads | same host option normalization and required-option precedence | use fromTracker; retain every missing/file/dangling source and parent, stable path-free refusal and preserved bytes |\n| corpus output conflicts refuse before source or bounds reads without exposing paths | same required-option precedence | use fromTracker so existing-output refusal executes before source/bounds; retain existing file, dangling link and directory cases |\n| corpus output inside the source refuses before inventory reads through relative and symlink aliases | same required-option precedence | use fromTracker; retain all direct, relative and symlink containment refusals with no source/output writes |\n| containment rechecks, bounded fits, no-git corpus/intake and public improver building | same unsupported underscore-only SDK keys | use declared fromTracker/fromTrackers; keep real training, bounded reservations, sealed replay and immutable sources |\n| domain, benchmark, lineage and loop missing-option expectations | required flags now refuse in the host; missing-option code is absent (upstream candidate) | match exact host text, expected error shape, absent code, exit 2 and unchanged tracker; keep reachable whitespace handler refusals |\n| takeover and evaluation SDK option spellings | GH-1665 publishes canonical camel-case SDK keys and folds CLI spellings | use forceTakeover/evaluationCandidate and actual force-takeover spelling; remove underscore fallback reads that real CLI dispatch never supplies |\n\nValidation: corpus 17/17; other focused command checks 10/10; intake 8/8; release approval/calendar 31/31; production and test typechecking, lint, zero duplication across 64 sources, docstrings (572 declarations), publish attestation, identity audit, production audit (zero vulnerabilities), pack dry-run and isolated strict health with required merge drivers pass. Reverting only stringOption in a disposable copy makes the canonical-source regression fail (1/1 fails); restoring it passes (1/1). The four takeover fallback branches were removed because supported CLI dispatch only supplies forceTakeover; both real CLI and SDK spellings remain covered. Required string guards remain reachable via whitespace values and are retained.\n\nFull npm run release:check, bun run release:check and unchanged 100/100/100/100 coverage scope are deferred to CI under the explicit 45-minute local budget: the measured Dependabot npm/Bun jobs took 78/62 minutes. These full local gates were not run and no full coverage certification is claimed. No thresholds, seed counts, deadlines or assertions were lowered; no other tracker item or recursive-training epic was changed. The two upstream candidates are recorded separately and were not filed."
  "2026-11-14T09:44:36.511Z",codex-toolchain-1114b,"Linked npm run changelog:check passes via pm test --run --progress. Claim is released; the item remains in progress for orchestrator verification. Regenerate and check the changelog after this final tracker write. Full exact-head npm/Bun and coverage certification remains required in CI."
  "2026-11-14T09:49:17.801Z",codex-toolchain-1114b,"CI dispatch receipt for migration head ab7d23d74d6033013166a81b769210019300c743: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/actions/runs/43582118483; CodeQL https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/actions/runs/43582118450. Full npm (Node 22/26), Bun (Node 26), and unchanged four-dimension 100 percent coverage certification await CI. This is dispatch evidence, not a passing result. Record the run before the final check; this tracker-only snapshot regenerates the changelog and the resulting pushed head requires fresh exact-head CI evidence. Claim remains released and the item stays in progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-11-18T10:49:49.399Z",codex-sol,"Round CA: all three prior jobs report 99.98% branch coverage. Merge main, identify and exercise the missing behavior, regenerate the changelog and run direct gates."
  "2026-11-18T10:57:00.639Z",codex-sol,"Merge commit 1ab85a6 reconciles both lockfiles and preserves the main-branch path decoding and pm-ops version. Node 22, Node 26 and Bun logs all pinpointed the same two verdict decoders. Exact-value decoding preserves the supported SDK and CLI spellings, invalid-value refusals and immutable replay identity."
  "2026-11-18T11:03:24.240Z",codex-sol,"Both real verdict suites pass 37/37 on Node 26. Typecheck, production and test builds, lint, docstrings, duplication, changelog regeneration/check and the Bun 1.3.14 frozen lockfile pass. The full-file quick-depth coverage run is in progress; the known pm-rl-streamtiming pipe deadline recurred and its unchanged isolated test passes 1/1."
  "2026-11-18T11:04:26.308Z",codex-sol,Implementation commit bde81fe follows merge 1ab85a6. The generator removed the empty Unreleased heading in the current tag projection. The Bun lock now matches the merged Babel and ESLint pins and passes the CI-pinned frozen install. PR 174 supersedes Dependabot PR 172; orchestrator owns its disposition.
  "2026-11-18T13:54:27.287Z",codex-sol,"Round CF: verify the published host option contract, fix the corpus dashed-key regression, and run the package gates for PR #174."
  "2026-11-18T13:58:14.654Z",codex-sol,The published pm-cli v2026.11.8 notes list GH-1665. The v2026.11.7 npm build lacks the extension option normalizer and v2026.11.8 includes it. Use the first supporting host floor consistently and require a corpus source diagnostic on a fresh destination for both declared spellings.
  "2026-11-18T14:02:20.414Z",codex-sol,"Node 26 typecheck and lint passed. After refreshing origin tags, changelog regeneration and changelog:check passed with identical tracked output. The published v2026.11.2 and v2026.11.7 loaders both refused the built extension at its new manifest floor with their current and required host versions."
  "2026-11-18T14:07:58.970Z",codex-sol,Published npm hosts v2026.11.8 and v2026.11.14 loaded the built extension. PmClient.run delivered dashed and camel corpus options to the path-aware source check on a fresh output. An ambiguous controller refused normal resume and dashed force-takeover then promoted one generation and recorded a redacted holder audit on both hosts.
  "2026-11-18T14:09:15.968Z",codex-sol,"CodeRabbit PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs649DvD and PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs649DvX map to b3bb5dfa62cb (host floor, loader refusal and audited force takeover). PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs649Dvf maps to b3bb5dfa62cb (fresh-output corpus option regression)."
  "2026-11-18T14:09:24.834Z",codex-sol,The three new regression checks passed on Node 26. Test typechecking and lint passed after switching the existing audited takeover fixture to its dashed spelling. The full-file direct tests and 100 percent coverage gate are still running.
  "2026-11-18T14:11:36.824Z",codex-sol,"The specific merged verdict option test passed. The Node 26 regression set passed 3/3, including old-host compatibility, fresh-output corpus source reads, and redacted takeover history. The direct broader suite and full-depth coverage gate continue alongside the PR's normal CI. The previous PR head completed the Node 22 quick and four-dimension coverage gates."
  "2026-11-18T14:38:34.671Z",codex-sol,"Normal CI run 44321702602 on pushed head 805103e43dad passed all four Node 26 shards, the merged 100 percent gate for lines, branches, functions and statements, the Node 26 aggregate and release checks. Node 22 shard 1 passed and shard 2 failed. The three edited regressions passed directly on both Node versions. The direct full-depth coverage run hit the existing callback fault matrix watchdog and was stopped. Its unchanged isolated rerun passed 123 of 123 including all 122 injected faults. Existing item pm-rl-local-gate-timing tracks local acceptance timing."
  "2026-11-18T14:41:51.971Z",codex-sol,The Node 22 shard-2 log has one failure. The unchanged packed two-generation CLI test in test/process-cli.test.ts hit spawnSync ETIMEDOUT. Its isolated Node 22 run also hit the same timeout. The changed tests are assigned to the successful shard 1. Merged coverage reported 64 authored files and 100 percent in all four dimensions.
  "2026-11-18T14:46:12.333Z",codex-sol,"Round CG will compare the packed CLI on origin/main and the published PR head under Node 22 and Node 26, then verify any timing fix against the required gates."
  "2026-11-18T14:48:50.793Z",codex-sol,"Run 44321702602, job 134862060843, identifies the initial rl loop run child at test/process-cli.test.ts line 20. Package installation had already succeeded. The unchanged watchdog is testTime(20000) and quick CI uses the default multiplier of one. The fetched main revision independently reproduces the failure in the same test, so the PR is not required to trigger it."
  "2026-11-18T14:49:50.590Z",codex-sol,"The candidate raises only the initial two-generation child watchdog to testTime(60000), matching the existing install watchdog base. Product resource allowances and every packed acceptance assertion are preserved."
  "2026-11-18T14:50:51.199Z",codex-sol,"Unmodified test wall times at scale 1, using each revision’s npm lockfile: main 6b6dcf8 on Node 22.23.4 43.73s and on 26.13.0 42.43s; PR 805103e on Node 22.23.4 51.59s and on 26.13.0 48.85s. All four fail at the initial child watchdog, so these wall times include setup and cannot measure uncensored loop throughput. Node 26 typecheck, build, build:test, lint, and changelog:check passed for the candidate."
  "2026-11-18T14:57:05.412Z",codex-sol,"With PM_TEST_TIME_SCALE=3 and only install timing added in disposable checkouts, all four pre-fix comparisons pass. Main versus PR on Node 22: wall 108.20s versus 89.41s, loop 47.81s versus 35.22s, install 3.84s versus 5.51s. On Node 26: wall 64.23s versus 66.44s, loop 26.83s versus 27.46s, install 3.39s versus 3.01s. The installed SDK versions use identical minimum-version evaluation logic, a comparison against the current version supplied to it. The PR is not required to hit the preexisting loop watchdog, and the measurements do not show a consistent runtime slowdown."
  "2026-11-18T14:58:33.513Z",codex-sol,"Round CG fix, Give the packed process acceptance child a scaled watchdog, preserves CF evidence commit 46deaa3. The complete edited test file passes 1/1 on Node 22.23.4 (73.24s wall, 38.52s loop) and 1/1 on Node 26.13.0 (34.15s wall, 13.71s loop), at the default scale of one. There are no other test files that reference the edited file. Node 26 build, typecheck, build:test, lint and changelog:check pass. The local quick coverage gate is running and exact-head CI will collect and merge its four normal coverage shards."
  "2026-11-18T21:34:08.212Z",codex-sol,"Round CQ: merged the main branch through ea1dcd8 without conflicts and retained the branch evidence commits. Verify quick shard coverage, run the focused gates on Node 22, and publish the branch update through its normal PR checks."
  "2026-11-18T21:34:45.764Z",codex-sol,"The linked 37-test verdict replay now explicitly uses test concurrency 2, matching the recorded run for PR #174 thread PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs65D4a1."
  "2026-11-18T22:16:38.028Z",codex-sol,"Round CQ Node 22.23.4 gates: typecheck, production and test builds, lint, and regenerated changelog check passed. The launcher assigned all 91 quick test files once across 14, 42 and 35 files. The workflow and shard contract passed 6/6. The corrected gatesim and leaderboard replay passed 37/37, the separate lifecycle verdict contract passed 29/29, and the changed-file regression suite passed 262/262 including packed process acceptance. These direct runs had no failures, skips or cancellations."
